From: TB371FC entry reconstruction study
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] arm64: distinguish the kexec reset wrapper from vendor ABI

Base: tem423/android_kernel_lenovo_tb371fc
      9d8abebf4ac4d45cf4cc11b5b6bc5e4483d10fd1

The vendor arch/arm64/mm/proc.S exports a two-argument cpu_soft_restart.
Kexec's cpu-reset.h declares an unrelated four-argument static inline with
the same name. Give the kexec wrapper a unique name; keep the legacy symbol
and the five-register __cpu_soft_restart assembly helper unchanged.

This is newly reconstructed code, not a recovered historical 0015 patch.
Compilation is not proof of a working handoff on the tablet.

--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/cpu-reset.h
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/cpu-reset.h
@@ -16,7 +16,7 @@
 void __cpu_soft_restart(unsigned long el2_switch, unsigned long entry,
 	unsigned long arg0, unsigned long arg1, unsigned long arg2);
 
-static inline void __noreturn __nocfi cpu_soft_restart(unsigned long entry,
+static inline void __noreturn __nocfi cpu_soft_restart_kexec(unsigned long entry,
 					       unsigned long arg0,
 					       unsigned long arg1,
 					       unsigned long arg2)
--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/machine_kexec.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/machine_kexec.c
@@ -207,7 +207,7 @@
 	local_daif_mask();
 
 	/*
-	 * cpu_soft_restart will shutdown the MMU, disable data caches, then
+	 * cpu_soft_restart_kexec will shutdown the MMU, disable data caches, then
 	 * transfer control to the reboot_code_buffer which contains a copy of
 	 * the arm64_relocate_new_kernel routine.  arm64_relocate_new_kernel
 	 * uses physical addressing to relocate the new image to its final
@@ -215,7 +215,7 @@
 	 * relocation is complete.
 	 */
 
-	cpu_soft_restart(reboot_code_buffer_phys, kimage->head, kimage->start, 0);
+	cpu_soft_restart_kexec(reboot_code_buffer_phys, kimage->head, kimage->start, 0);
 
 	BUG(); /* Should never get here. */
 }
